🟢 1. Environment Variables
✅ How to Set
Linux/macOS Terminal:

bash
Copy
Edit
export SERVER_PORT=9090
Windows Command Prompt:

cmd
Copy
Edit
set SERVER_PORT=9090
Spring Boot automatically maps environment variables like SERVER_PORT to server.port.

✅ How to Get in Java
You can access environment variables using:

java
Copy
Edit
@Value("${server.port}")
private int port;
OR use Spring’s Environment API:

java
Copy
Edit
@Autowired
private Environment env;

public void getEnvValue() {
    String port = env.getProperty("server.port");
    System.out.println("Port: " + port);
}



🟢 2. Command-Line Arguments
✅ How to Set
When running your JAR:

bash
Copy
Edit
java -jar myapp.jar --server.port=8085 --spring.datasource.username=admin
Spring Boot treats them just like environment variables and binds them automatically.

✅ How to Get
Same as above:

java
Copy
Edit
@Value("${server.port}")
private int port;
Spring Boot merges command-line args > env vars > config file, so this overrides anything in application.yml.



🟢 3. Default Values in Code
If a config is not present from any source, you can provide a default value directly using:

java
Copy
Edit
@Value("${myapp.mode:default-mode}")
private String mode;
If myapp.mode is missing, this will fall back to "default-mode".

✅ Precedence Order (Highest to Lowest)
Command-line arguments

Environment variables

application.yml / application.properties

Default value in code using @Value(...:default)

🔁 Real Example (All Together)
🔹 application.yml
yaml
Copy
Edit
myapp:
  title: "Default App"
  port: 8080
🔹 You override via command-line:
bash
Copy
Edit
java -jar app.jar --myapp.title="CLI App"
🔹 You access it like:
java
Copy
Edit
@Value("${myapp.title:Untitled App}")
private String title;


🔹 Result:
If CLI arg is present → "CLI App"

Else if env var is set → that value

Else if in .yml → "Default App"

Else → "Untitled App"

💡 Pro Tip
You can also use @ConfigurationProperties and set defaults directly in the class:

java
Copy
Edit
@ConfigurationProperties(prefix = "myapp")
@Component
public class AppConfig {
    private String mode = "default-mode";  // default if not set anywhere

    // getter/setter
}
